<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gutalag</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gutalagen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gutalag is the medieval law code of Gotland, written in the Old Gutnish language, probably in the thirteenth century. It sets out the rules of the island's self-governing farmers, covering church matters, inheritance, compensation for injuries and the duties of the islanders. It survives in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> of about 1350, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gutasaga">Gutasaga</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gutalag.jpg" alt="Gutalag" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown. Editor: Patrik Granholm · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holm_B_64_17_f._2r_Guta_lag_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
